WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
Thanks for tuning in to Tesla Short's time, episode 534 for July 7th, 2026.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.700
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.380
Let's dive into today's Tesla news.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.080
NHTSA's plan to drop mandatory brake pedals opens a path for RoboTaxi's built without

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.820
driver controls from day one.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:26.400
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is proposing to eliminate a 31-year-old rule.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.860
That rule assumes every vehicle has a human driver ready to brake at any moment.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.520
The change would allow manufacturers to design RoboTaxi's without redundant brake hardware

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.140
components.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.260
Certification would move towards system-level redundancy instead of duplicate physical parts.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.880
Final adoption would reshape how future unsupervised fleets are built and inspected.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.500
This regulatory step directly affects production planning for models like the CyberCab.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.620
Now shifting to the first vehicle that could use this new path.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.760
Tesla introduced a longer wheelbase Model YL with a genuine third row sized for adults.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.280
The layout targets six and seven-seat crossover buyers rather than occasional use.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.320
Production timing and pricing stay tied to the current Model Y refresh cycle.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.000
Official range and cargo figures are still pending ahead of showroom arrival.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.580
The Model positions Tesla against legacy family haulers from traditional automakers.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.720
A buyer in California placed the first order for the new Model YL.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.080
The local Tesla Center called the same day with launch event details.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.720
Delivery timing stays open while production ramps up.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.700
Early orders like this will give the first real-world data on wait times for the extended version.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.720
Meanwhile, Tesla is also opening its battery lines to outside teams.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.020
Giga Berlin launched the Cell Giga Challenge for battery startups.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.540
Selected teams receive paid pilot runs on the 4,680 line.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.920
The program moves beyond unpaid trials to direct funding and production scale data.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.640
The goal is fresh yield and cost ideas that could feed into European structural packs.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.280
Output from the trials could influence cell specifications for the next vehicle programs there.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:23.140
This effort builds on earlier supplier outreach but adds concrete production access.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.880
Internal targets at the same site point to a 20% rise in weekly output from existing lines

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:35.740
through efficiency gains alone. European demand signals remain the key variable for sustaining

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:42.440
that higher rate. As Tesla experiments with cell supply, it is also adjusting prices in markets where

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:49.280
subsidies just began. Tesla raised Model Y and Model 3 prices in South Korea shortly after

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.920
qualifying for local battery electric vehicle incentives. Critics say the increases largely cancelled

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.740
the buyer benefit from the subsidies. The company has not commented on the timing or the size of

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:07.880
the adjustments. Regulators may review whether the program is achieving its intended price reduction.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.080
The pattern shows how quickly posted prices can absorb most of an incentive.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:18.540
Now turning to the broader question of how subsidies function as margin timing tools.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:24.520
Subsidies shift when manufacturers adjust prices more than they change underlying costs.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:30.060
South Korea shows posted prices can absorb most of the incentive within days.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.480
Realized margins therefore become partly a function of regulatory calendars.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:42.040
The same logic applies when incentive shrink or disappear. A price cut that looks generous can

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:47.840
simply restore the pre-substitied equilibrium. Buyers who focus only on the headline incentive

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.740
miss how quickly the manufacturer recalibrates. Factories still need to hit cost targets,

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.720
yet the realized price per unit can swing with subsidy calendars.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:03.400
Watching the next round of qualification deadlines gives a clearer signal on near-term margin

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.920
pressure. Service also began in a limited Miami zone following the Texas launch.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:15.360
The expansion tests scaling of the app and remote monitoring team. Utilization rates are being

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.780
watched to gauge whether the initial rollout supports broader valuation assumptions.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.780
The CyberCab was presented as a purpose-built robotaxi without traditional controls.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.360
The design emphasizes fleet economics over individual ownership.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.920
Early displays focused on interior space and sensor layout rather than performance specs.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.480
While policy and pricing play out, real-world autonomy incidents continue to surface.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:47.000
A driver was recorded fully asleep at highway speed while the vehicle maintained speed.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.960
The cabin camera captured the occupant with no strong intervention from the system.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:58.140
Tesla will need clearer escalation protocols before unsupervised operation can expand.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.320
Separate legal action against another autonomy developer adds pressure on the sector.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:09.600
A separate incident recorded a driver asleep at 100 km per hour on an open road.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:15.420
Current cabin camera systems issued no intervention strong enough to wake the occupant.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.680
Safety questions sit alongside the latest software tweaks riders are already seeing.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:25.720
The Robotaxi app now shows whether a safety driver is present on the trip.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:31.320
Riders see a clear indicator before the ride begins so they know if supervision is active.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:36.180
The feature covers Texas operations and any new cities added this summer.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.020
It aims to set clearer expectations while supervised service continues.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.700
Feedback from users will shape how the company communicates capability limits going forward.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:53.900
This update addresses rider expectations around current supervised operation versus future unsupervised

00:05:53.900 --> 00:06:00.220
service. On the sales front, battery electric vehicle registrations doubled in Japan during the

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:06.140
first half of the year. Registrations of battery electric vehicles rose sharply through June

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:12.320
compared with the same period last year. Tesla captured meaningful share behind Toyota and ahead

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:18.340
of Nissan in the segment. Growth came across multiple price points rather than a single high volume

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:23.620
model. Continued expansion will depend on charging access outside major cities.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:30.240
Tesla and Rivian both posted higher second quarter deliveries while several legacy automakers saw

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:36.100
electric vehicle volumes decline. Both companies posted higher second quarter handovers while

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:42.500
several traditional automakers saw EV volumes decline. The divergence points to differences in

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:48.820
inventory management and model availability. Financing partners noted steady demand for the newer

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:54.460
entrance despite higher interest rates. The trend will be tested again when third quarter numbers

00:06:54.460 --> 00:07:00.780
arrive. Owners report growing appreciation for over-the-air updates, sentry mode, and cabin

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:07.520
preconditioning after the first year. The list also includes front utility and the mobile app remote

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:13.460
control functions. Survey responses came from long-term drivers rather than new buyers.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:18.760
Continued software improvements will determine whether these features keep widening the gap

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:25.240
versus competitors. Tesla is selling summer gear including a powered cooler that fits in the model

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:32.520
Y frunk or trunk. The powered cooler fits inside the model Y frunk or trunk and runs on the vehicle's

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:38.420
12 volt system. Other items include a peril and accessories tied to the current vehicle lineup.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:44.580
The move extends Tesla's direct to consumer sales beyond cars into lifestyle products.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:50.680
Sales volume will show whether owners treat the store as a regular stop. An owner who switched from

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:56.540
full-size pickup tracked fuel maintenance and electricity costs. The owner tracked fuel,

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:02.680
maintenance, and electricity costs after switching from a full-size pickup. Savings appeared mainly

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:08.780
in daily commuting rather than towing or long haul use. The comparison covered several months of

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:15.460
real-world operation across mixed routes. Broader adoption among truck buyers will hinge on similar

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:22.580
transparent cost data. Before we go, keep an eye on how the new model YL wait times developed from

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:31.460
those early California orders. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $419.77

